---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/privy-vs-drip';
const title = 'Privy vs Drip for Shopify Email: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "Compare capture and lifecycle ownership using a replenishment workflow with auditable product data.";

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does Drip offer popup capture?",
    "answer": "Yes. Its Onsite documentation describes popup formats and targeting, so include capture in the evaluation rather than automatically buying a second tool."
  },
  {
    "question": "When must a store leave Privy email?",
    "answer": "There is no universal order threshold. Document the required logic and evaluate whether the available configuration can support it."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I assume product metafields are workflow inputs?",
    "answer": "No. Inspect the supported Shopify data and any required custom mapping before designing branches around those fields."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-[#5d3a1d]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#5d3a1d]">Privy vs Drip</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Privy vs Drip for Shopify email</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Compare capture and lifecycle ownership using a replenishment workflow with auditable product data.</p>
      </header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>A workflow requirement is a better trigger than order count</h2>
        <p>Consider a hypothetical coffee roaster selling different bag sizes alongside gifts. It needs useful replenishment reminders without nudging gift buyers to reorder for themselves. This is a proposed scenario, not an observed merchant outcome. Privy markets capture and messaging together. Drip documents workflows and Onsite forms, so the choice should include whether Drip can cover both jobs rather than assuming Privy must remain.</p>
        <h2>Write the replenishment rule before the canvas</h2>
        <p>Specify the qualifying purchase, the product identifier and the reason for the delay. Do not promise that a Shopify metafield automatically becomes an available workflow property. Ask for the actual payload or supported field mapping in your account. Where consumption timing is unknown, start with a preference request or educational message rather than inventing a precise reorder date.</p>
        <h2>Exercise gift and repeat-purchase paths</h2>
        <p>In a proposed controlled rehearsal, use a personal purchase, a gift purchase and a second order placed before the reminder. The gift path should use the chosen gift indicator rather than guessing from a different delivery address. A new purchase should change the pending reminder according to the written rule. Record what the workflow actually does when the second event arrives late.</p>
        <h2>Assess Drip capture as well as imported subscribers</h2>
        <p>Drip Onsite documentation covers targeted popup formats; describing it as only basic embedded forms would exclude a real option. If you already use Privy, compare keeping its signup experience with consolidating capture. Preserve the acquisition source and offer eligibility. A second tool is worthwhile only if the retained experience or operating benefit exceeds the cost and handoff burden.</p>
        <h2>Inspect the workflow as an operator</h2>
        <p>Have the person who will maintain the program find the entry event, delay, exclusion and exit rule. Then propose a new roast that should not receive the standard reminder. Check how they would change the rule without disturbing existing participants. Workflow visibility is useful only if the operator can explain the active audience and has access to the underlying data.</p>
        <h2>Measure and price the whole program</h2>
        <p>Compare contribution from the intended customer cohort after discounts and returns, keeping attribution separate from demonstrated lift. Obtain current quotes for your audience and sending needs, including a capture subscription if retained. Include the effort to map fields, maintain branches and resolve failed events. No monthly order count, capture-rate percentage or assumed lost revenue establishes a universal migration deadline.</p>
        <h2>Decision and cutover</h2>
        <p>Evaluate Drip when the replenishment logic and its ongoing maintenance are the actual buying questions. Retain Privy if its capture or messaging path serves a requirement that consolidation would compromise. Assign the welcome and replenishment triggers to one owner each and rehearse purchase exclusion before switching senders. These are proposed checks; this comparison contains no measured workflow speed, recovery rate or revenue result.</p>
        <h2>Primary documentation</h2>
        <p>Product scope checked against primary material on November 25, 2026. Documentation establishes advertised capabilities, not results for this store.</p>
        <ul><li><a class="link" href="https://www.privy.com/">Privy product scope</a></li><li><a class="link" href="https://help.drip.com/hc/en-us/articles/12920842128269-Getting-Started-Overview">Drip getting started</a></li><li><a class="link" href="https://help.drip.com/hc/en-us/articles/39439950367885-Onsite-Pop-ups-vs-Embedded-Forms">Onsite versus embedded forms</a></li></ul>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-drip">Omnisend vs Drip</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-privy">Omnisend vs Privy</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/food-and-beverage">Email apps for food &amp; beverage</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Privy vs Drip FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
